  "english": "THE YEARLY LETTER: [Gg - Գ]\n\nTHE ROMAN SEVEN-DAY LETTER: 4\n\nJanuary [rendered from text confusion]\n20. Tuesday. Tone 1 [AK]. [Feast of the] Sukiasiank [St. Sukias and companions]. Father [Hymn] tone 1 [adz]: \"We praise You, righteous.\"\n25. Sunday. Tone 7 [DZDZ / DZ]. Mid-Lent [Mijink]. Hambartsi [Hymn of Ascent] tone 7 [gdzing / DZ]: \"The Resurrection.\" See according to the order in the First Volume, up to Vardavar [Feast of the Transfiguration], keeping the order of this place.\n\nFebruary [rendered from text confusion]\n1. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Eve of Great Lent [Boon Barekendan].\n14. Saturday. Tone 5 [GZ]. Of the fast. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnndaraj].\n21. Saturday. Tone 4 [BK]. St. Cyril Patriarch of Jerusalem, and the other Cyril, and his mother Anna, and the Patriarchs John [Yovhannes] of Jerusalem, John [Yovhannes] of Odzun, John [Yovhannes] of Vorotn, and Gregory [Grigor] of Tatev.\n\nMarch\n22. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADZ]. Easter [Zatik]: Feast of the Resurrection of Christ our God.\n\nApril\n7. Tuesday. Tone 2 [ACH / AJ]. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin Mary.\n30. Thursday. Tone 8 [DK]. Feast of the Ascension of Christ our God into heaven.\nSee according to the order in the First Volume.\n\nJanuary\n5. Tuesday. Tone 4 [BK]. Nativity and Epiphany of Christ.\nThe post-feast eating days [Mijots Outik] is six days.\n11. Sunday. Tone 1 [ADZ]. Eve of the Fast of Catechumens [Barekendan Arajavorats]. Sixth Day of the Nativity of Christ.\n12. Monday. Tone 2 [AK]. Of the fast. Seventh Day of the Nativity of Christ.\n13. Tuesday. Tone 3 [BDZ]. Of the fast. Eighth Day of the Nativity of Christ.\n14. Wednesday. Tone 4 [BK]. Of the fast. Father [Hymn] of Penance, tone 1 [adz]: \"They sang.\"\n15. Thursday. Tone 5 [GZ]. Of the fast. Father [Hymn] of Penance, tone 2 [ak]: \"Glorified forever.\"\n16. Friday. Tone 8 [DK]. Commemoration of Jonas the Prophet.\n17. Saturday. Tone 7 [DZ]. Feast of the Birth of Saint John the Forerunner [Karapet].\n18. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Of the Resurrection. Father [Hymn] tone 7 [dz]: \"Glorifying.\" Hambartsi [Hymn of Ascent] tone 8 [dk]: \"Glory to the Resurrection.\"\n19. Monday. Tone 1 [ADZ]. [Feast of St.] Sarkis and his son Martiros, and the fourteen soldiers, and the Atomian Generals.",
